<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>Rulealize.Registry.Catalogue</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No reference to Rulealize, and that is the point rather than an omission. This tool never
    loads a plugin: PluginProbe loads into the default context so that a plugin's
    Rulealize.Abstraction resolves to the one already in memory, which is right for a host and
    means one process cannot hold two versions of the same plugin assembly. So the catalogue
    runs tool/Ledger once per version instead, in a process of its own, and reads its output.

    What is left here is fetching and arranging, which needs nothing but the framework.
  -->

</Project>
